{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/973073-garou-and-the-astral","id":973073,"title":"Garou and the Astral","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-20T06:04:56-07:00","id":973073,"title":"Garou and the Astral","content":"So what is wrong with using a lot of the mage otherworlds as potential story ideas in Werewolf. I recall reading Infinite Tapestry and being all like, Damn all this stuff would be hella interesting for more then just the Stargazers.<br /> <br /> The idea of collecting Boons that last for an entire Umbral Quest for instance is a brilliant idea for weaving a Legend!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T06:10:50-07:00","id":973080,"title":"","content":"Don't see why not, just gotta figure out the legitimate way to get there. I heard climbing Weaver's webs is dangerous but possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12132-bogdan","name":"Bogdan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T10:33:50-07:00","id":973220,"title":"","content":"im more concerned how much the umbra intersects the astral plane, how vulnerable is an astrally projected Vampire or psychic to a Garou's claws.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T11:49:16-07:00","id":973267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/973073-garou-and-the-astral?p=973220#post973220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">im more concerned how much the umbra intersects the astral plane, how vulnerable is an astrally projected Vampire or psychic to a Garou's claws.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming they're is the same place, very.<br /> <br /> But most the time (in my experience) the Astral Plane is ruled to be the High Umbra's Penumbra, and therefore a completely different spiritual realm than the Garou (Middle Umbra) Penumbra. There is some debate surrounding that, but that is the way I've seen the Spirit worlds interpreted the majority of the time.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T13:36:50-07:00","id":973355,"title":"","content":"This is litterally covered by the most recent Umbra book. Garou take damage equal to their rage entering the Astral. Garou don't naturally enter the Astral. Yes Vampires flirt around in the &quot;penumbra&quot; of the astral, and if a Garou were in the right place at the right time they could cut the Vampire's cord, BUT that's just about as likely as finding their physical form and killing that while they are out, perhaps less so because the whole garou have trouble entering the Astral(and leaving it) vs their naturally being in the material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T13:37:56-07:00","id":973356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/973073-garou-and-the-astral?p=973267#post973267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Assuming they're is the same place, very.<br /> <br /> But most the time (in my experience) the Astral Plane is ruled to be the High Umbra's Penumbra, and therefore a completely different spiritual realm than the Garou (Middle Umbra) Penumbra. There is some debate surrounding that, but that is the way I've seen the Spirit worlds interpreted the majority of the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is correct, as of the revised version of the Storyteller's Handbook for Werewolf Apocalypse it had been ruled in the crossover section the &quot;astral realms&quot; depicted in Auspex's Psychic Projection were to be assumed to be the Shadowlands, the Dark Umbra's Penumbra; however, as of W20 Umbra, the Velvet Shadow, it's now the Astral Umbra (High Umbra):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astral Umbra</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a Garou travels through the Astral Umbra, he may witness the ghostly forms of vampires floating about tethered to thin silver cords. This is not the physical body of the vampire, it is a thought projection and capable of small amounts of interactions with the Umbra.<br /> <br /> Most vampires spend much of their time in the Astral Umbra peering through into the physical realm. Unless the vampire is particularly astute, she tends to ignore her Umbral surroundings. She perceives a thin, watered down version of the Astral Umbra overlaid on top of the physical world. Vampires rarely engage with other entities within the Astral \u2014 such as other vampires, Garou, or Mages \u2014 as her capabilities in dealing with them are limited by her will and mastery of the Auspex Discipline. A stealthy Garou can pass most vampires without attracting notice, unless of course he attempts to disrupt the silver cord trailing behind one.<br /> <br /> The silver cord is the vampire\u2019s lifeline back to her body, and she will defend it as best she can versus attack. Vampires are capable of a basic kind of assault, usually attempting to cut the silver cord of other mentally projected travelers. If there is no cord, the vampire has little recourse for an attack. Of course, smart vampires flee at the first sight of a werewolf shining in their muted perceptions.</div> </div> </div> </div>It goes on to say the Astral Umbra is anathema to them as the Rage of a werewolf irritates the Astral, causing it to warp and become hostile towards the entering Garou. The distinction of it being completely different than the Middle Umbra's Penumbra is given when it suggests a few ways a Garou could employ to enter the Astral Umbra:<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;...A traveler could pass through the Membrane into the Astral from the Deep Umbra where the two meet at highly conceptual realms. This means the traveler has to delve into some strange and alien realm of the Deep Umbra, pass whatever dangers lie there, to come to the Astral in a deeply conceptual realm \u2014 only to find her physical form drawn into strange ideals.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Alternatively, and perhaps even more restrictive:<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;...Some scholars believe that by meditation and thought they can enter the Astral Umbra from any part of the Umbra. This practice has met with limited success. The only place anyone has been able to meditate to enter the Astral is within the Stargazer\u2019s Homeland. Through meditation on thoughts and ideas a Stargazer is able to send a mental projection into the Astral, leaving her body behind. This seems to be the safest way to travel, though the werewolf loses any concept of time and body as her mind travels through strange realms, carrying a danger of death through negligence.&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12152-rotwood","name":"Rotwood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T14:15:26-07:00","id":973382,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12152-rotwood\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12152\" data-vbnamecard=\"12152\">Rotwood</a>, as long as you are quoting rules (and I'm assuming have the pdf on hand) can you quote the rule for Garou taking their Rage in damage for entering the Astral Plane?<br /> <br /> It does seem like (even during Revised) they hadn't nailed down exactly how all of the Spirit Worlds interacted. I'm glad they are finally ironing out the details. Even still, it almost seems purposeful that they gave everyone their own special Umbras to reduce crossover problems.<br /> <br /> Also, for getting to the Astral Plane/High Umbra there was a Stargazer Gift, and probably some Rites here or there. I know the Mokole had some High Umbra stuff in their book. That's the book (from memory) that first statedthat the Garou Deep Umbra was the Mage High Umbra, which is why I'm guessing that the Vampire's Astral Plane was then made to be in the Dark Umbra.<br /> <br /> Edit to add: While Garou have some difficulties getting to the Astral Plane, it would be a much easier task to summon a Spirit that would be able to pass over to clear out any Astral spies. Plenty of middle Umbra spirits would have connections enough with the High Umbra to be able to accomplish such a task (Chimera's brood comes to mind).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 09-20-2016, 05:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T14:38:21-07:00","id":973396,"title":"","content":"I couldn't find any quote that made mention to a system of damage in the book, this is the only quote where I found a reference to a Garou's Rage in regard to the Astral Umbra:<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;The Astral is a place of ideas and concepts, not physical realities. On a purely conceptual level, the substance making up a traveler is subject to the same vagaries as any other concept within the Astral. A traveler could very well end up disparate pieces of himself, floating about the Astral with no way to return to his normal state. <b>Even worse is that the Rage of a werewolf irritates the Astral, causing it to warp and become hostile towards the entering Garou.</b></i><br /> <br /> As for summoning a spirit to scrape the Astral Umbra, that might be viable, though a vampire daring to spy on Garou (with enough Auspex (R5), might as well be a Tremere trying to study them since Auspex is one of their clans disciplines), Path of Spirit Manipulation (the third power, in specific) could potentially foil with said attempt to keep Astral scriers away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12152-rotwood","user":"Rotwood","date":". 09-20-2016, 05:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12152-rotwood","name":"Rotwood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T15:02:22-07:00","id":973415,"title":"","content":"As of W20 Umbra, the Deep Umbra and the Astral are not the same thing. The Deep Umbra lies beyond the Membrane, while the Astral is a region of the Near Umbra primarily visited by Stargazers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T15:43:56-07:00","id":973447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/973073-garou-and-the-astral?p=973382#post973382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Edit to add: While Garou have some difficulties getting to the Astral Plane, it would be a much easier task to summon a Spirit that would be able to pass over to clear out any Astral spies. Plenty of middle Umbra spirits would have connections enough with the High Umbra to be able to accomplish such a task (Chimera's brood comes to mind).</div> </div> </div> </div>Make sure they check every animal for a random subsume! The Dark Umbra for ghosts and put lots of beaded doors up to catch anyone with obfuscate!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T16:10:29-07:00","id":973462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rotwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/973073-garou-and-the-astral?p=973396#post973396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I couldn't find any quote that made mention to a system of damage in the book, this is the only quote where I found a reference to a Garou's Rage in regard to the Astral Umbra:<br /> <br /> <i>&amp;quot;The Astral is a place of ideas and concepts, not physical realities. On a purely conceptual level, the substance making up a traveler is subject to the same vagaries as any other concept within the Astral. A traveler could very well end up disparate pieces of himself, floating about the Astral with no way to return to his normal state. <b>Even worse is that the Rage of a werewolf irritates the Astral, causing it to warp and become hostile towards the entering Garou.</b></i><br /> <br /> As for summoning a spirit to scrape the Astral Umbra, that might be viable, though a vampire daring to spy on Garou (with enough Auspex (R5), might as well be a Tremere trying to study them since Auspex is one of their clans disciplines), Path of Spirit Manipulation (the third power, in specific) could potentially foil with said attempt to keep Astral scriers away.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. At that point you are talking about a specific Clan with a specific path of Thaum. And really, if your little spirit doesn't come back, either send a bigger one or let the brood resolve the problem themselves.<br /> <br /> I actually like the idea of the Penumbras overlapping enough to interact (an idea they've moved away from) since it better explains why different Supernaturals can't just spy on each other. With this setup, there is no reason (or little reason) for vampires not to be completely informed of the goings on at their local Cearn. Same goes for ghosts and Mages and then the Changers in relation to others.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/973073-garou-and-the-astral?p=973447#post973447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Make sure they check every animal for a random subsume! The Dark Umbra for ghosts and put lots of beaded doors up to catch anyone with obfuscate!</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that it matters, but subsumed animals should be easily detectable with Primal Urge. The Penumbral overlaps would take care of the ghost issue, and Obfuscate doesn't work so well on Caerns since there are spirit guardians. As much of a point as you are trying to make by being sarcastic, none of the spiritual fortresses (Caerns, Nodes, Chantries, etc.) in the WoD should be vulnerable to just walking in spiritually. If they are, that leaves giant gaps in the setting for why things run the way they do.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 09-20-2016, 07:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T11:44:18-07:00","id":973951,"title":"","content":"no sure many high umbra spirits like werewolves, or mid umbra spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T12:01:14-07:00","id":973961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rotwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/973073-garou-and-the-astral?p=973356#post973356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It goes on to say the Astral Umbra is anathema to them as the Rage of a werewolf irritates the Astral, causing it to warp and become hostile towards the entering Garou...</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bI wonder if that means that Rage-less shapeshifters (like the Nuwisha, for instance) would have an easier time with Astral travel. Given how adamant the Garou are about being the end-all-be-all of the spirit realms, wouldn't<i> that </i>be ironic?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T12:21:02-07:00","id":973967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/973073-garou-and-the-astral?p=973961#post973961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> \u200bI wonder if that means that Rage-less shapeshifters (like the Nuwisha, for instance) would have an easier time with Astral travel. Given how adamant the Garou are about being the end-all-be-all of the spirit realms, wouldn't<i> that </i>be ironic?<br /> </div> </div> </div> </div>More appropriate the ironic since the Nuwisha taught the garou how to step sideways. The Nuwisha and Corax are the most learned of the spiritworlds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T15:13:28-07:00","id":974058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/973073-garou-and-the-astral?p=973967#post973967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> More appropriate the ironic since the Nuwisha taught the garou how to step sideways. The Nuwisha and Corax are the most learned of the spiritworlds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, according to the Nuwisha at any rate. And while that <i>may</i> be true (anything the children of Coyote say should be taken with <i>some</i> degree of skepticism), the Corax <i>have</i> Rage, so they should be expected to have all the same problems with the Astral as the Garou.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T17:37:10-07:00","id":974134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/973073-garou-and-the-astral?p=974058#post974058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, according to the Nuwisha at any rate. And while that <i>may</i> be true (anything the children of Coyote say should be taken with <i>some</i> degree of skepticism), the Corax <i>have</i> Rage, so they should be expected to have all the same problems with the Astral as the Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Corax are more likely to have low Rage and/or precautions against it.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, this business with the astral harming beings that enter it physically is new to W20. Previously, the Mokole were the most prominent astral travelers among the Garou and Fera.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T18:37:47-07:00","id":974163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/973073-garou-and-the-astral?p=974134#post974134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Corax are more likely to have low Rage and/or precautions against it.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, this business with the astral harming beings that enter it physically is new to W20. Previously, the Mokole were the most prominent astral travelers among the Garou and Fera.</div> </div> </div> </div>So asking you then, since I didn't get an answer earlier. Can you give a page reference for taking Rage in damage for entering? I can't find any such rule in the Astral Umbra section of the book. It only says &quot;Even worse is that the Rage of a werewolf irritates the Astral, causing it to warp and become hostile towards the entering Garou.&quot; with no system set up as far as I can tell.<br /> <br /> I too, am used to the idea of Mokole somewhat regularly frequenting the Astral (High) Umbra.<br /> <br /> And having read the section myself now, getting to the Astral Plane shouldn't be overly difficult (though not easy) if you go through the Dream Zone first. It's certainly an extra step, but relatively safe as far as traveling through the Umbra proper can be. And getting into the Dream Zone is actually really easy.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T18:44:05-07:00","id":974170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/973073-garou-and-the-astral?p=974163#post974163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So asking you then, since I didn't get an answer earlier. Can you give a page reference for taking Rage in damage for entering? I can't find any such rule in the Astral Umbra section of the book. It only says &quot;Even worse is that the Rage of a werewolf irritates the Astral, causing it to warp and become hostile towards the entering Garou.&quot; with no system set up as far as I can tell.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't actually mean to suggest that there was a system for it, sorry. I don't know what, exactly, it's intended to be, either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I too, am used to the idea of Mokole somewhat regularly frequenting the Astral (High) Umbra.<br /> <br /> And having read the section myself now, getting to the Astral Plane shouldn't be overly difficult (though not easy) if you go through the Dream Zone first. It's certainly an extra step, but relatively safe as far as traveling through the Umbra proper can be. And getting into the Dream Zone is actually really easy. </div> </div> </div>Especially for Mokole, it seems in W20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T19:03:41-07:00","id":974178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/973073-garou-and-the-astral?p=973355#post973355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> This is litterally covered by the most recent Umbra book. Garou take damage equal to their rage entering the Astral.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly just quoting <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2715\" data-vbnamecard=\"2715\">Lian</a> to see if they have a page reference for this or if it's just a head canon extrapolation from the line &quot;Even worse is that the Rage of a werewolf irritates the Astral, causing it to warp and become hostile towards the entering Garou.&quot;.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/973073-garou-and-the-astral?p=974170#post974170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't actually mean to suggest that there was a system for it, sorry. I don't know what, exactly, it's intended to be, either.</div> </div> </div> </div>At this point, since 2 others (besides myself) have said they haven't heard of taking physical damage, I'm inclined to think it's a house rule interpretation (and I will certainly change my mind if I see something that says differently). So the &quot;new&quot; Astral Umbra might not actually be that far off of how it was in Revised, save that Vampires actually project into it specifically now, which is kind of odd on the one hand since the W20 Umbra book goes on to say that they don't really perceive the Astral plane terribly well without really trying (assuming they actually know to try).<br /> <br /> So yea, no reason not to have Mokole doing their thing in the High Umbra still.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T04:09:39-07:00","id":974979,"title":"","content":"Without the W20 and it reworking of the Umbra I always assumed the following:<br /> <br /> The Stargazer gift &quot;Astral Mind&quot; brings one to the same penumbra-like area of the Astralplane as does Auspex or the Astral Projection psi numina.<br /> Since I always found it kind of stupid, that a being in the dark umbra or astralplane could just walk into a caern and go unnoticed, since werewolf only deals with the middle umbra and all gifts and rites are worded that way I allowed for garou in specially warded areas to see a outline of beings currently in dark or Astral umbra in the middle umbra, too. This allowed them to attack these shadow like representations and eventually drive them of, ending psycho projection and powers like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T12:09:53-07:00","id":975157,"title":"","content":"I would rule that it is part of the nature of the Garou to take damage from their Rage when they enter the High Umbra, not the nature of the Rage of the other Fera (who are not the Warriors of Gaia). For example the Mokole, who are designed to enter the High Umbra whenever they wish, should not be penalized. Now, as a side note, you can also take the Balor Roads (from Changeling) to reach the High Umbra. While that means that you have to have a Changeling friend to enchant you, take you into the Near Dreaming, and send you on your way, it may actually be less dangerous than any other methods suggests.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T21:34:54-07:00","id":975368,"title":"","content":"I always assumed that Epiphlings and even Banes like Kalus were actually spirits from the Astral Plane that somehow entered the Gaian Penumbra. I've been giving a lot of thought as to what the Astral Plane actually is and the creatures who live there, and how they intersect with the Gaian Penumbra, but I've never become satisfied. So it is something I am still working on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T09:23:06-07:00","id":975551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/973073-garou-and-the-astral?p=975157#post975157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would rule that it is part of the nature of the Garou to take damage from their Rage when they enter the High Umbra, not the nature of the Rage of the other Fera (who are not the Warriors of Gaia). For example the Mokole, who are designed to enter the High Umbra whenever they wish, should not be penalized. Now, as a side note, you can also take the Balor Roads (from Changeling) to reach the High Umbra. While that means that you have to have a Changeling friend to enchant you, take you into the Near Dreaming, and send you on your way, it may actually be less dangerous than any other methods suggests.</div> </div> </div> </div>The don't take damage by the rules, though. In fact, it just sounds like Rage pisses off the Astral and produces scenes of conflict, not some kind of Avatar Storm thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T00:02:43-07:00","id":975861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/973073-garou-and-the-astral?p=974178#post974178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mostly just quoting <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2715\" data-vbnamecard=\"2715\">Lian</a> to see if they have a page reference for this or if it's just a head canon extrapolation from the line &quot;Even worse is that the Rage of a werewolf irritates the Astral, causing it to warp and become hostile towards the entering Garou.&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was misremembering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}